syndrome (specificity).", "background": "Down's syndrome occurs when a person has three, rather than two copies of      
chromosome 21; or the specific area of chromosome 21 implicated in causing Down's syndrome. It is the commonest         
congenital cause of mental disability and also leads to numerous metabolic and structural problems. It can be           
life‐threatening, or lead to considerable ill health, although some individuals have only mild problems and can lead    
