          {"study_index": 602, "title": "Higher median levels of free ß‐hCG and PAPP‐A in the first trimester of        
  pregnancy in a Chinese ethnic group. Implication for first trimester combined screening for Down's syndrome in the    
  Chinese population", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE To study the effect of ethnic Chinese on the medians of free beta-hCG     
  and PAPP-A in the first trimester of pregnancy. METHODS The data of 943 women undergoing first trimester combined     
  screening for fetal Down syndrome were analysed to derive the Chinese-specific medians. The calculated risk of Down   
  syndrome based on these Chinese-specific medians was compared with that based on the original algorithm of the Fetal  
  Medicine Foundation (FMF). RESULTS The maternal serum levels of multiples of median of free beta-hCG and PAPP-A were  
