population", "abstract": "OBJECTIVE To study the effect of ethnic Chinese on the medians of free beta-hCG and PAPP-A in 
the first trimester of pregnancy. METHODS The data of 943 women undergoing first trimester combined screening for fetal 
Down syndrome were analysed to derive the Chinese-specific medians. The calculated risk of Down syndrome based on these 
Chinese-specific medians was compared with that based on the original algorithm of the Fetal Medicine Foundation (FMF). 
RESULTS The maternal serum levels of multiples of median of free beta-hCG and PAPP-A were significantly higher among the
Chinese than among the Caucasians. The weight-adjusted gestation-specific medians were developed. Without adjustment for
ethnicity, the original FMF algorithm underestimated the risk of Down syndrome by a median of 1%. Adjustment by         
ethnicity increased the false-positive rate by 10% (from 5.3 to 5.9%). CONCLUSION Ethnic Chinese have a significantly   
