(sensitivity or detection rate) and the proportion of women with a low risk (normal) screening test result who          
subsequently had a baby unaffected by Down's syndrome (specificity).",                                                  
        "selection_criteria": "We included studies in which all women from a given population had one or more index     
test(s) compared to a reference standard (either chromosomal verification or macroscopic postnatal inspection). Both    
