=== BATCH SCREENING TASK ===
Review: First trimester serum tests for Down's syndrome screening
Total studies to screen: 18

SELECTION CRITERIA:
We included studies in which all women from a given population had one or more index test(s) compared to a reference 
standard (either chromosomal verification or macroscopic postnatal inspection). Both consecutive series and diagnostic 
case‐control study designs were included. Randomised trials where individuals were randomised to different screening 
strategies and all verified using a reference standard were also eligible for inclusion. Studies in which test 
strategies were compared head‐to‐head either in the same women, or between randomised groups were identified for 
inclusion in separate comparisons of test strategies. We excluded studies if they included less than five Down's 
syndrome cases, or more than 20% of participants were not followed up.

INSTRUCTIONS: For each study below, decide INCLUDE or EXCLUDE.
Return exactly one decision object per study; do not omit excluded studies, do not summarize exclusions in bulk, and do 
not return only included studies.
